1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
-[eagle screeching]
-[whimpering]

2
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
[King] What is this creature?

3
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

4
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:14,000
[singer singing in English]

5
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

6
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

7
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
[singer singing in English]

8
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
[singer singing in Japanese]

9
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
TAKING STOCK X AND X TAKING ACTION

10
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
[birds chirping]

11
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
[narrator] One day remains
before the sorting,

12
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Hey. Good morning.

13
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Up already? It's kinda early.

14
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:33,000
[Killua] Nineteen hours
till midnight on sorting day.

15
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
We make our move tonight.

16
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Right. Let's do one final check.

17
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
[map beeping]

18
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Once we're in, Gon and I will head up
the central stairway to the throne room.

19
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
If you find her, escape without us.

20
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
You got it.

21
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
If the King and his three Royal Guards

22
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:09,000
You're really hung up on that, aren't you?

23
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Yeah, what are the chances?

24
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
It's pretty unlikely.

25
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:18,000
[Killua] It is, but you've gotta admit
unlikely things happen all the time.

26
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
We did a bunch of research
on the enemy's behavior

27
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
and used it to decide when to attack.

28
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
When you think you know
exactly where and when

29
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
you can expect someone to be,
more often than not,

30
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
that's when the unexpected happens.

31
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,000
It was pretty common in my old job.

32
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
We don't have that luxury.

33
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
As soon as we make a move,
there's no turning back.

34
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
We need to plan for every scenario
and decide what we would do.

35
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
[Killua] They might not be
in the throne room,

36
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
but if they're still in the palace,
it's okay.

37
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Pitou's En is enough to cover the palace,

38
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:15,000
the surrounding courtyards, and then some.

39
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
So as soon as we enter,

40
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:22,000
we need to see if we can sense
that creepy aura anywhere close by.

41
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
That'll tell us
whether or not they're there.

42
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Then we just follow that aura
to where it feels the most dense.

43
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Oh!

44
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Right. That's what I can't figure out.

45
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
The Royal Guard
never leaves the King's side,

46
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
so if Pouf was there,

47
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
I'm positive the other two
were in the palace with the King too.

48
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Well, then we should ask Colt himself.

49
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,000
[Killua] Yeah.

50
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:35,000
[Colt] I'd guess Pitou was giving
someone medical attention.

51
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,000
[Killua over phone] What?

52
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
I did tell you that Pitou was the one
who repaired Kite, didn't I?

53
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
In hindsight, I don't believe
Pitou used En during that time.

54
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
Healing must require
a great deal of concentration.

55
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,000
who would have had the skills
to injure them?

56
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Good question.

57
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,000
An internal dispute?

58
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Maybe the King injured
one of the Royal Guards for some reason?

59
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:22,000
No. No, that's impossible.

60
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
and that's never gonna happen.

61
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
But I guess the bigger question now is
who was it that injured the King?

62
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:51,000
The Royal Guard would never harm him,
and you could rule out the underlings too.

63
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
They'd never so much as
put a scratch on him.

64
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[Gon over phone] You're right,
and that's why we're pretty sure…

65
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,000
He injured himself?

66
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Wait. How could that have happened?

67
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
We don't know what's going on here yet,
but it's all we've got.

68
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
-[Ikalgo grunts]
-[Killua] Mmm-hmm.

69
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
[line disconnects]

70
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:17,000
but that chance
wouldn't have been possible

71
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
under normal circumstances.

72
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:00,000
It looks like their march
has begun at last.

73
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Ten hours until midnight,
when the sorting starts.

74
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:14,000
five million humans
will fill the palace grounds.

75
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
They may try
to use the celebration as a cover

76
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:46,000
is that the King may somehow
be spirited away beyond our reach.

77
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Let's just say that one of them
has the ability to teleport objects.

78
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
The King's been irritated enough with us

79
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:13,000
because of how close
we've been covering him as it is.

80
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:16,000
Then we guard him secretly
without his knowledge.

81
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:20,000
The only problem with that
is that we need someone

82
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:22,000
close enough to monitor his surroundings

83
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Meow all of the enemy presences
have completely disappeared.

84
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
And I can't sense
any residual aura from them whatsoever.

85
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
They must be using Zetsu
to hide amongst the marching humans.

86
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Hey. What's up?

87
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[Knuckle] There are so many people.

88
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Looks like they had
about a hundred per building.

89
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
They all must have been packed inside.

90
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Then if we all conceal our presences,

91
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
they'll be forced to assume that
we're hiding somewhere among the citizens.

92
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Do you think there's any chance

93
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
they'll decide
to cancel the march altogether?

94
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:28,000
No. No way.

95
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:32,000
That would mean delaying
or even canceling the entire celebration,

96
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:36,000
which would imply the King
had accepted defeat and compromised.

97
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:46,000
So the celebration is gonna begin
as scheduled, tomorrow at 3:00 p.m. sharp,

98
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:49,000
and there's not a damn thing
we can do to stop it.

99
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
[Neferpitou sighs]
Once the humans started to move,

100
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:56,000
my puppets couldn't
tell them apart anymore.

101
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Well, what do you think?
Should I recall them right meow?

102
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,000
No. Giving the enemy free rein
would be simply ridiculous.

103
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
[groans]

104
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[Morel] It's just like we thought.

105
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
The Nen puppets have joined the march.

106
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:51,000
We'll have to avoid the front entrances
due to heightened security,

107
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:06,000
So what? Are you getting scared?

108
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:09,000
That's absurd. I just don't want
to be caught off guard, okay?

109
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Waiting by the entrances
for the right moment

110
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
since the Ants can pick up on the signal.

111
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:52,000
you shouldn't take their security net
too lightly.

112
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
-[Knov] I'll handle it.
-Huh?

113
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:57,000
[Knov] I'm the only one among us

114
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
who can enter and exit these rooms
whenever I please.

115
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:03,000
I'll keep you all informed.

116
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
For now, you should rest here.

117
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,000
You sure you'll be okay?

118
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
I'm just keeping watch.
I can't imagine that'll be a problem.

119
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:18,000
I'll be close,
but right outside of Pitou's En range, so…

120
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
That's exactly what Kite ran into.

121
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Yeah, he probably did that deliberately.

122
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Not a single one of you
can strike fear in me like they do.

123
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
I won't take any risks…

124
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:08,000
ever again.

125
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Any person who leaves their line
will be shot on sight.

126
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Move out!

127
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Pitou.

128
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:38,000
You knew that Komugi was being attacked,
did you not?

129
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Yes. I was monitoring the area with En.

130
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:47,000
However, I saw no threat to you, sire,
so I ignored it.

131
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
From this point on,
you'll keep an eye on Komugi as well

132
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,000
and deal with any threats at once.

133
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Yes, as you wish.

134
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
heading toward the King…

135
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,000
just like ants.

136
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
No, lemmings.

137
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Wait a second. What is that?

138
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Every one of them
looks completely vacant, dazed.

139
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Those scales must have a hypnotic effect.

140
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
Stay in line as you advance!

141
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Do not leave this line!

142
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Once you're in position,
wait for orders, and don't move!

143
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:28,000
[Knov] Simple orders repeated on a loop
while tanks roll in the background

144
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:33,000
can easily seep into a mind
exhausted from hours of marching.

145
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:49,000
obedient till the end,
when it's their turn.

146
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,000
[snoring]

147
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[Morel] Hypnosis? I see.

148
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:04,000
-Huh?
-We won't have to worry

149
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,000
about the whole crowd
flying into a total panic

150
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
if the battle
starts to get out of control.

151
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,000
This is a really big deal.

152
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:22,000
And assuming that over half of the people
will be in place at midnight

153
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,000
waiting for the sorting process
to get started,

154
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Now we can fight all we want.

155
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
[grunts]

156
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
[Shoot] They both look so calm.

157
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
It's like he's overflowing
with confidence.

158
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,000
But I can't help but wonder,

159
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,000
why is it that,
now and then, he seems so sad?

160
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Out of everyone here,

161
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
I'm the one suffering
from the most anxiety.

162
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:34,000
The fate of humanity
rests on my shoulders.

163
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
[Knuckle] Colt is a good guy.

164
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Meleoron and Ikalgo,
they both have good hearts.

165
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:46,000
It doesn't matter
if they're humans or Ants.

166
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Everyone has a heart.

167
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
That has to be true.

168
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:13,000
by defeating that Ant.

169
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:16,000
[Killua] He's fired up.

170
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:32,000
All these battles are taking their toll.

171
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
On a scale of 1 to 100, I'm about 40.

172
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
No, 35.

173
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Can't cry about it now.

174
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
With Knov out, I'm the only one left.

175
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
I'd hoped to fight at full strength,

176
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:52,000
but it's much easier
to accept my fate this way.

177
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
[Knov] I'm sorry, Morel, everyone.

178
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:07,000
[shudders] But I…

179
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
I can't face them again.

180
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
I'll go check on the palace.

181
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
[Meleoron] So two minutes
is about the longest I can hold my breath.

182
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Given how tense I'll be,

183
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
my limit will probably be half that
at best.

184
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:32,000
It's fine.
A minute is more than enough time.

185
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
Thank you for that, Killua.

186
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:16,000
[King] I am King.

187
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
But who am I, really?

188
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
Our time's up. Let's go.

189
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,000
[Gon] Palm.

190
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:08,000
[narrator] Ten minutes remain
until they enter the palace.

191
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
[singer singing in Japanese]
